Section 9.1 registry form: topic 1 must be the transaction's sender's 20 bytes
preceded by 12 zero bytes. A contract calls the declared registry, which names
msg.sender, so topic 1 is the contract. Everything else about the log is
well-formed and the hash does sit in the transaction's calldata at a readable
offset; the log is still no anchor, and nobody is charged for a third party's
call under their own transaction.
